Venetium 0075 - VP9 and AV1 files play again on Windows ARM32 (a fix for 0066).
Found 2026-11-21: WebM (VP9 / AV1) files did not play at all on ARM32 - local files, <video src>, Wikimedia, WebM clips
on sites. FFmpegDemuxerStream::Create() checks every track with IsDecoderSupportedVideoType(VideoType::FromDecoderConfig()),
and FromDecoderConfig() has to guess a level because a file does not declare one: it picks the lowest (VP9 10, AV1 20).
The ARM32 codec steering (0055/0066) refuses every VP9 / AV1 type that carries a level, so each file track looked like a
codec string with a level and was dropped ("skipping invalid or unsupported video track"). Sites that use MSE (YouTube)
were not affected: their codec strings go through isTypeSupported / canPlayType, which is what the steering is for.
Now a demuxed VP9 / AV1 track counts as level-less while kVenetiumArm32CodecSteering is on, as 0066 intended, so files
play (in software); the steering of the codec strings that sites ask about is unchanged. x86 is unchanged
(the feature is off there), and --disable-features=VenetiumArm32CodecSteering still turns the whole steering off.

diff --git a/media/filters/ffmpeg_demuxer.cc b/media/filters/ffmpeg_demuxer.cc
index 45d82a3..7896ada 100644
--- a/media/filters/ffmpeg_demuxer.cc
+++ b/media/filters/ffmpeg_demuxer.cc
@@ -87,6 +87,22 @@
   return stream->disposition & AV_DISPOSITION_DEFAULT;
 }
 
+// Venetium 0075: VideoType::FromDecoderConfig() has to guess a level (a file
+// does not declare one) and picks the lowest, so every demuxed VP9 / AV1 track
+// looked like a codec string with a level. The Windows ARM32 codec steering
+// (0055/0066) refuses those so that sites pick H.264 - and so every VP9 / AV1
+// file (<video src>, local files, WebM clips) failed to play. A file's track
+// counts as level-less here, as 0066 intended; the steering of the codec
+// strings that sites ask about (isTypeSupported / canPlayType) is unchanged.
+VideoType VenetiumDemuxedVideoType(const VideoDecoderConfig& config) {
+  VideoType type = VideoType::FromDecoderConfig(config);
+  if ((type.codec == VideoCodec::kVP9 || type.codec == VideoCodec::kAV1) &&
+      base::FeatureList::IsEnabled(kVenetiumArm32CodecSteering)) {
+    type.level = kNoVideoCodecLevel;
+  }
+  return type;
+}
+
 }  // namespace
 
 static base::Time ExtractTimelineOffset(
@@ -236,7 +252,7 @@
     if (!AVStreamToVideoDecoderConfig(stream, video_config.get()) ||
         !video_config->IsValidConfig() ||
         !IsDecoderSupportedVideoType(
-            VideoType::FromDecoderConfig(*video_config))) {
+            VenetiumDemuxedVideoType(*video_config))) {
       MEDIA_LOG(DEBUG, media_log) << "Warning, FFmpegDemuxer failed to create "
                                      "a valid/supported video decoder "
                                      "configuration from muxed stream, config:"
